1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:06,481
Walked. Saw. Didn't see. Mia is telling us about yesterday, and she is using the past simple.

2
00:00:07,081 --> 00:00:14,155
By the end of this lesson, you will be able to tell any story about the past, clearly and correctly. Let's start.

3
00:00:15,105 --> 00:00:25,119
Here is the good news. The past simple is the same for every person. I walked, you walked, she walked, they walked. No extra s, no changes.

4
00:00:25,719 --> 00:00:29,994
For most verbs, we just add e d. Walk becomes walked.

5
00:00:30,594 --> 00:00:32,061
Play becomes played.

6
00:00:32,661 --> 00:00:34,254
Watch becomes watched.

7
00:00:34,854 --> 00:00:36,683
Visit becomes visited.

8
00:00:37,283 --> 00:00:41,143
Remember: the same form for I, you, he, she, it, we and they.

9
00:00:42,243 --> 00:00:51,568
Let's watch Mia's evening again. Yesterday evening, Mia walked through the grass. She stopped near the sheep, and she counted them: one, two, three.

10
00:00:52,518 --> 00:00:58,110
Now, let's practise your speaking. Listen, and repeat after me. Say it out loud!

11
00:00:59,010 --> 00:01:00,593
I walked to the hills.

12
00:01:03,593 --> 00:01:05,079
She saw three sheep.

13
00:01:08,129 --> 00:01:11,430
Number 1. Yesterday I blank to the market.

14
00:01:17,230 --> 00:01:19,823
Went. Go is irregular: go, went.

